---
description: Useful context for tests.
globs: 
alwaysApply: false
---
When creating new tests, always create a configuration class that will handle all of the environment variables. 

When creating tests, always make sure to have a Setup and Tear Down function that will set up a new test database, migrate and then tear it down and clean the data at the end. 

Properly manage the database session in the test fixtures. Ensure that test data is handled properly and checks that only are needed for production only happen in production. 

Make sure to set the application context whenever you need to. 